<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<ns0:example xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167829859398">
<ns0:exercise id="fs-id1167833137652">
<ns0:problem id="fs-id1167836619820">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836619822">For the function <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mo stretchy="false">(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo stretchy="false">)</ns1:mo><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>−</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>5</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> evaluate the function.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836320931"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mo stretchy="false">(</ns1:mo><ns1:msup><ns1:mi>h</ns1:mi><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn></ns1:msup><ns1:mo stretchy="false">)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> <ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mo stretchy="false">(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo stretchy="false">)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> <ns0:span class="token">ⓒ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:para>
</ns0:problem>
<ns0:solution id="fs-id1167833397154">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836754871"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> <ns0:newline />
<ns0:table id="fs-id1171790386499" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="g of x = 3 x minus 5. To evaluate g of h squared, substitute h squared for x. g of h squared = 3 times h squared minus 5. Simplify. g of h squared = 3 h squared minus 5.">
<ns0:label />
<ns0:tgroup cols="2">
<ns0:colspec colnum="1" colname="c1" />
<ns0:colspec colnum="2" colname="c2" />
<ns0:tbody>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1171792580809" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed on a white background, reading g(x) = 3x - 5, representing a linear function."><ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_018a_img_new.jpg" /></ns0:media></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">To evaluate <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:msup><ns1:mi>h</ns1:mi><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn></ns1:msup><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> substitute <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:msup><ns1:mi>h</ns1:mi><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn></ns1:msup></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> for <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>.</ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1171790163372" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed on a white background: g(h^2) = 3h^2 - 5. The variable 'h' is highlighted in red, indicating its specific role within the function."><ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_018b_img_new.jpg" /></ns0:media></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1171792588637" alt="A mathematical equation shows g(h squared) equals 3h squared minus 5, representing a function where the input and the variable in the expression are both h squared."><ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_018c_img_new.jpg" /></ns0:media></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
</ns0:tbody>
</ns0:tgroup>
</ns0:table></ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836556251"><ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> <ns0:newline />
<ns0:table id="fs-id1171792580965" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="g of x = 3 x minus 5. To evaluate g of the quantity x plus 2, substitute x plus 2 for x. g of x plus 2 = 3 times the quantity x plus 2 in parentheses minus 5. Simplify. g of x plus 2 = 3 x plus 6 minus 5. g of x plus 2 = 3 x plus 1.">
<ns0:label />
<ns0:tgroup cols="2">
<ns0:colspec colnum="1" colname="c1" />
<ns0:colspec colnum="2" colname="c2" />
<ns0:tbody>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1171792545190" alt="A mathematical equation for a linear function, g(x) = 3x - 5, is displayed in black text on a white background."><ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_019a_img_new.jpg" /></ns0:media></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">To evaluate <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> substitute <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> for <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>.</ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1171792543055" alt="The equation g(x + 2) = 3(x + 2) - 5 is displayed, showing a function transformation where the input (x) is replaced by (x + 2) in a linear function."><ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_019b_img_new.jpg" /></ns0:media></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">Simplify.</ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1171792802121" alt="The image displays a mathematical equation, g(x + 2) = 3x + 6 - 5, presented in a black font on a white background."><ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_019c_img_new.jpg" /></ns0:media></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1171790304229" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed: g(x + 2) = 3x + 1, against a white background."><ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_019d_img_new.jpg" /></ns0:media></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
</ns0:tbody>
</ns0:tgroup>
</ns0:table></ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836448921"><ns0:span class="token">ⓒ</ns0:span> <ns0:newline />
<ns0:table id="fs-id1167836606104" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="g of x = 3 x minus 5. To evaluate g of x plus g of 2, first find g of 2. g of 2 = 3 times 2 minus 5. g of 2 = 1. Now find g of x plus g of 2. g of x plus g of 2 = 3 x minus 5 plus 1. The 3 x minus 5 is from g of x and the 1 is from the g of 2. Simplify. g of x plus g of 2 = 3 x minus 4.">
<ns0:label />
<ns0:tgroup cols="2">
<ns0:colspec colnum="1" colname="c1" />
<ns0:colspec colnum="2" colname="c2" />
<ns0:tbody>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167829839522" alt="The mathematical function g(x) = 3x - 5 is displayed.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_020b_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">To evaluate <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> first find <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836635207" alt="A mathematical equation shows 'g(2) = 3 * 2 - 5', with the number 2 highlighted in red in both instances.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_020c_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167829685715" alt="The image displays a mathematical equation, g(2) = 1, presented in a clear, digital format on a plain white background.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_020d_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836693279" alt="A mathematical expression asks to 'Now find g(x) + g(2)'.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_020a_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836322927" alt="Equation g(x) + g(2) = 3x - 5 + 1, where 3x - 5 is identified as g(x) and 1 as g(2) by blue underbraces.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_020e_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">Simplify.</ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167824734809" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed, showing 'g(x) + g(2) = 3x - 5 + 1' in black text on a white background.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_020f_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836539801" alt="The image shows a mathematical equation in black text on a white background. The equation is 'g(x) + g(2) = 3x - 4'.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_020g_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
</ns0:tbody>
</ns0:tgroup>
</ns0:table></ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167832981642">Notice the difference between part <ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> and <ns0:span class="token">ⓒ</ns0:span>. We get <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mo stretchy="false">(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo stretchy="false">)</ns1:mo><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>1</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> and <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>−</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>4</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> So we see that <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mo stretchy="false">(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo stretchy="false">)</ns1:mo><ns1:mo>≠</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>g</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:para>
</ns0:solution>
</ns0:exercise>
</ns0:example>

